Kind: ablation
Issue: #659
Takes out: turning a refused AMD engine off again -- the read-back's refusal returns with IommuEn set, as before 59fdbd48, the device table entries pointing at tables the boot then counts as not in use: every pin and slot it routes in the old format is target-aborted
Run: --iommu amd-xt --entry 48 900 -smp 4
With: 659-widen-gaen-ignored.patch
Expect: delivered 0 while masked and 0 once routed to vector 0x40 — WRONG
Note: QEMU cannot show this, and its Run is QEMU's: Rev 3.11 says IommuEn=0 means "no upstream transactions are translated or remapped", and QEMU 11.1.1's amdvi_int_remap_msi() remaps through the device table whatever IommuEn says -- it asks only that a table is set and the entry's IV -- so under QEMU the fixed tree, which turns the engine off, loses the pins and slots as the ablated one does, and both print the Expect (on GitHub, run 38205921729: 8 of 8 each). On bare metal with an AMD engine that ignores GAEn the fixed tree's interrupts arrive; with the widen alone the boot also says "interrupt remapping COULD NOT BE TURNED ON — WRONG", as it should

